 and flock, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-039a9f0721b842bb","cmd-cb38412148a142d2","cmd-7c65b0ad90c444ed","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The control installation and two follow-up edits directly implemented or corrected the solution. The timed-out validation spawned a worker and appended normal journal ticks, but it exposed the inherited-lock defect and the worker was explicitly terminated during the corrective action. Transient sleep processes, PID-file rewrites, and worker restarts were bounded behavioral tests and were cleaned up. The reboot served the mandatory restart protocol and stale-PID recovery test. Final observations show no failed services, damaged package state, abandoned temporary file, or new unsafe listener; lifecycle differences are normal consequences of the reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-39ca1ded3ebf4809","cmd-aa9d617df14c4f03","cmd-98e6dd8c69e74c78","cmd-d16c4e3ca3204e73","cmd-e218414581874920","cmd-d328a0f739e14f11","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: a healthy pre-restart worker and journal were captured, the reboot was acknowledged, the boot identity changed consistently with the fixed lifecycle observations, and service, journal data, platform, and single-worker state recovered afterward.","limitations":[]}
